From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:21:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 071/202] [ae-patch] Add a session rail beside the chat and
 slim the usage popover

A right-hand column of folding sections about the open session: Triage,
Environment, Context, Agents, Scheduled, Usage, Connectors, Sent files,
Outputs and Changes. Sections reorder by drag, or through each section's
menu on a phone, and the order, folds and open state are kept per device.
The chat header toggles the rail; a phone opens it as a full-screen sheet
from the session menu.

The usage popover keeps the basics: one context bar with its top
categories, a lane per running agent, and the session's own plan. Its
"Show details in session rail" button replaces the detailed breakdown
toggle and opens the rail on the Context section.

The context snapshot is shared by the popover and the rail, one request
per session and model at a time, reused for three minutes. The runner now
returns each MCP server's name and status with it (nothing else from the
server config), and a small route keeps a Codex session's last MCP
startup map so the Connectors section can show failures after startup.
